# Writing content

Runbook: `src/data/writing-articles/README.md`.

## Single source of truth

- Each post: `src/data/writing-articles/<id>.json` (id, title, kind, year, excerpt, blocks)
- Archive order: `src/data/writing-articles/columns.json` → `essays` | `notes` | `talks` id arrays
- `writingArticles.ts` loads `*.json` (skips `columns.json`), resolves stills, builds `writingColumns`
- `writing.ts` only re-exports list helpers — **do not** put entry metadata there

## Archive UI (`Writing.tsx`)

- **Desktop (`lg+`)**: three columns (essays / notes / talks) side by side.
- **Mobile**: horizontal tabs for the same three categories; one list visible at a time. Don’t stack all three lists.

## Editor (`WritingEditor.tsx`)

- Click row → open pocket editor; `openId` drives active row highlight.
- **Close + clear selection**: Esc, red traffic-light, or **click backdrop** (always pointer-events when open) → `onClose` → `setOpenId(null)`.
- Chrome: traffic lights only (no title string next to them).
- **Toolbar** (font/align/dim tools): **desktop only** — `hidden lg:flex`. Don’t reintroduce on mobile.
- Opening sets shell `overlayOpen` so the mobile bottom nav hides.

## Add a post

1. Create `writing-articles/<id>.json` (kebab-case id; never reuse).
2. Append `id` to the right array in `columns.json`.
3. Figures: file in `src/assets/writing/figures/` (or `shared/stills/` if also used on Home); block `"src"` = filename only (no `url` field).
4. Click row on `/writing` opens the editor.

## Blocks

```json
{ "type": "p", "text": "..." }
{ "type": "image", "src": "hero4.jpg", "alt": "...", "caption": "optional" }
```

## Do / don't

- ✅ Keep filename, JSON `id`, and `columns.json` entry in sync
- ✅ Edit metadata/body only in the article JSON
- ❌ Don’t revive `index.json` or duplicate list data in `writing.ts`
- ❌ Don’t hand-edit resolved image `url` fields
